@5095 = ~Potion of Heroism~
@5096 = ~Potions are typically found in ceramic, crystal, glass, or metal flasks or vials. Flasks or other containers generally contain enough fluid to provide one person with one complete dose to achieve the effects of the potion.

This one comes from another “universe.”

STATISTICS:

Maximum hit points: +25
Regeneration: 5 points per round
THAC0: +6
Armor class : +3
Duration: 10 turns

Weight: 1~
@5097 = ~Elixir of the Imperfect~
@5098 = ~Potions are typically found in ceramic, crystal, glass, or metal flasks or vials. Flasks or other containers generally contain enough fluid to provide one person with one complete dose to achieve the effects of the potion.

This one comes from another “universe.”

STATISTICS:

Regenerate 10 Hits Point per second
Recall of a 1st-level spell (arcanic and divine) the 1st second, then a 2nd-level spell on the 3th second, then a 3nd-level spell on the 5th second, and so on until a 8nd-level spell on the 15th second
Duration: 15 seconds

Weight: 1~

@5099 = ~Potion of Aura Cleansing~
@50100 = ~This potion prevents magical residue from lingering around the drinker. As a result, they can cast spells in quick succession without disruption.

STATISTICS:

Improved Alacrity
Duration: 1 turn

Weight: 1~

@50101 = ~Potion of Extreme Power~ //EE only
@50102 = ~This foul-smelling concoction exaggerates the odds in favor of the drinker.

STATISTICS:

Damage: +150%
Duration: 5 turns

Weight: 1~

@50103 = ~Elixir of Magica Incarna~
@50104 = ~Inside its bottle, this potion is constantly in motion. This is noticeable thanks to the numerous magical particles swirling around in the mixture. Anyone who drinks this elixir merges with the web and becomes an elemental of magic.

STATISTICS:

Immunity to magical weapons
Immunity to spells
Infinite spells
Duration: 1 turn

Weight: 1~

@50105 = ~Potion of Absolute Speed~
@50106 = ~This midnight blue potion allows the drinker to reach speeds far beyond known limits. In fact, the drinker becomes so fast that the world around them seems frozen and, even stranger, devoid of color, as if the colors themselves cannot reach them.

STATISTICS:

Time Stop
Duration: 5 rounds

Weight: 1~

@50107 = ~Potion of Life~
@50108 = ~This potion has the effect of the Resurrection spell if sprinkled on the body of a deceased person.

STATISTICS:

Resurrection
Area of effect: one dead character
Weight: 1~

@50109 = ~Anti-Magic Brouet~
@50110 = ~This flask must be thrown. It creates an area where all magic is dispelled at the point of impact, with a 100% chance of success, and leaves anti-magic residue on affected creatures that disrupts their ability to cast spells for 4 rounds (100% chance of failing to cast a spell in the first round, 75% in the second round, 50% in the third, and 25% in the fourth).

STATISTICS:

Range: 30 feet
Magic Purge
Area of Effect: 30 feet radius

Weight: 1~

@50111 = ~Filter of Sublimated Luck~
@50112 = ~This potion, filtered to bring out the best, alters fate in favor of the drinker.

STATISTICS:

Luck +5
Duration: 4 turns

Weight: 1~

@50113 = ~Sanset's Reflector~
@50114 = ~This concentrated power gives the drinker the ability to reflect all spells targeting them back at the caster. There is no limit to the number of spells that can be reflected.

STATISTICS:

Infinite spell reflection
Duration: 5 turns

Weight: 1~

@50115 = ~Potion of Disappearance~
@50116 = ~This potion causes the drinker to disappear. They become invisible, odorless, silent, and undetectable. They gain +4 to AC and saving throws and can freely attack or cast spells while remaining invisible. The Potion of Disappearance also protects against scrying, divination, and enhanced vision.

STATISTICS:

Camouflage
Duration: 2 turns

Weight: 1~

@50117 = ~Heart of Ice~
